{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1386 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6ce9f2d703b1ac47f2a2bb1b22b6c02719a96af9149088999748e2f9c60c2d18" :edb/db-before-t 1385 :edb/db-after-t 1386 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534698 50 #inst "2026-10-12T08:13:40.757Z" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164006 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433187 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164006 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433187 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433199 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164007 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433199 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164008 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433189 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164008 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433189 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433204 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186164009 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433204 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166508 1071 "![](images/07/075eca4fcc837dce57c4bcfba01047af3d72f15b80cd3fabfc7e5b00be83813d.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ \nFind the solution of the new system in terms of the parameter $s.$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166508 1071 "![](images/28/287223863402ec50768dee1bf0910226fbb0f9ee4818faaae4a0f1bd6121df26.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ \nFind the solution of the new system in terms of the parameter $s.$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166508 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\,\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\,\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\,\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\,\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\,\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\,\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the first equation, we have\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = (s+3)X_1(s) - 4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)\\,[(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4] & =4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4(s+1) & =4 \\\\ [(s+1)(s+3)-3]{X}_{1}(s) & =4+4(s+1) \\\\ s(s+4){X}_{1}(s) & =4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $X_2(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{2}(s) & =(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4 \\\\  & =(s+3)\\,(\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)})-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+3)(s+2)-4s(s+4)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}+5s+6)-4({s}^{2}+4s)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+20s+24-4{s}^{2}-16s}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nX_1(s) =\\dfrac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\n$$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166508 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L\\,{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L\\,{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L\\,{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L\\,{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}+L\\,{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL\\,{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}-L\\,{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the first equation, we have\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = (s+3)X_1(s) - 4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)\\,[(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4] & =4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4(s+1) & =4 \\\\ [(s+1)(s+3)-3]{X}_{1}(s) & =4+4(s+1) \\\\ s(s+4){X}_{1}(s) & =4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $X_2(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{2}(s) & =(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4 \\\\  & =(s+3)\\,(\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)})-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+3)(s+2)-4s(s+4)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}+5s+6)-4({s}^{2}+4s)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+20s+24-4{s}^{2}-16s}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nX_1(s) =\\dfrac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\n$$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166509 1071 "![](images/24/243212bee1e50c7ca289142dcc8a9b5ac4f6d06fe3715661e99ec2601c82bf45.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_1(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{4}{s} + \\dfrac{1}{s-6}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{20}{s} - \\dfrac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166509 1071 "![](images/8d/8da4fe8a52643867946a0818f3181fa57d6dc5b067155876e26689cb3fdde85e.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_1(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{4}{s} + \\dfrac{1}{s-6}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{20}{s} - \\dfrac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166509 1074 "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{20}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =20{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166509 1074 "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{20}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =20{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166510 1071 "![](images/0b/0be5433ffb8166a35fc9084c59116f77b223e25b85f939cb3c279f983939bc1f.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXXXXXXX}[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166510 1071 "![](images/3f/3fa8db8d4186569020d5805ac76eee4f92f1c261dd2acb2502409a9b2b6db56b.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXXXXXXX}[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166510 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{9{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=9L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=9{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166510 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{9{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=9L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=9{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186166930 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433217 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166930 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433219 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186166931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186433218 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167006 1050 1080.0 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167160 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167160 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167160 1071 "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t); x_{2}^{′}(t) =-x_{1}(t) + 3x_{2}(t),x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n$X_{1}(s) = L{x_{1}(t)} = \\frac{1}{s - 1}, X_{2}(s) = L{x_{2}(t)} = \\frac{1/2}{s - 1} - \\frac{7/2}{s - 3}$.\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t) =$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $e^{t} +$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $e^{3t}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186167160 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1\\cdot t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7/2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167163 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 true] [17592186167163 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.$" 13194139534698 17592186045417 false] [17592186167163 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-9={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-6=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=9 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-2){X}_{2}(s)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ 6(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-2)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-3s){X}_{2}(s) & =9-6(s-1) \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-6s+15 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =6-(s-2)\\cdot \\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6s(s-3)-3(s-2)(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\